<p class="lede">AwardHome — the digital trophy case for competitive dance —
opens to the public on <strong>September 15</strong>. Over 1.5 million awards
from 4,200+ events across 27 competitions, going back to 2011, all in one
permanent, searchable home.</p>

<p>If you're a <strong>dance family</strong>: your dancer's results are very
likely already here. Search their name, find their trophy case, and claim it —
claiming lets you complete the record, add card photos and thank-you notes, and
share award cards that look as good as the moment felt. Profiles are free, and
dancer pages are built with families of minors in mind: private by default
where it matters, moderated everywhere it counts.</p>

<p>If you run a <strong>studio</strong>: your studio's page is waiting too, with
every award we've found across the competitions you've attended. Claiming takes
about two minutes and unlocks the tools we wished existed when we ran a studio —
merge duplicate profiles, correct records, an embeddable awards widget for your
own website, and a season-planning directory of every circuit's upcoming tour
dates, sortable by distance, with calendar export. The annual results-curating
spreadsheet is officially retired.</p>

<p>If you're a <strong>competition organizer</strong>: AwardHome is where your
results live on after the ballroom empties. Organizer accounts put your
branding on the award cards families share and your tour dates in front of
studios planning their season. We'd love to work with you — reach us through
the <a href="/partners" style="color: var(--primary);">partners page</a>.</p>

<p>AwardHome is free for dancers, families, and studios. Between now and
September 15 we're in private beta, onboarding studios and organizers by
invitation — and on launch day, the doors open for everyone.</p>

<p>See you on the 15th.</p>
